A51 GPU: address space, jobs, recovery, boot-time WRITE_VALUE (a51gpu=3).

Second part of the Mali-G72 service (spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-
29-a51-gpu-kernel-service-design.md), ported from the S7's HeroGPU. AS0 in
the legacy Mali-LPAE format (as Linux Panfrost drives the G72), HeroGPU's
map (test pages 0x02000000, scratch 0x0a000000, user 0x40000000-
0x7fffffff), tables and test/scratch pages in a 64 MiB region at
0x8e0000000 outside XNU's RAM, one fixed L3 table per 2 MiB of the user
range. Jobs run one at a time under a mutex, polled (200 ms), with
Panfrost's JS_CONFIG for the G72 (flush clean+invalidate at both ends,
flush reduction); a faulted or stuck job is hard-stopped and the GPU
soft-reset if needed. a51gpu=2 brings it all up; a51gpu=3 also runs a
chain at an unmapped VA (expects a fault and recovery) and then the
WRITE_VALUE job. a51gpulog=1 logs every job. Exports HeroGPU's interface
(herolte_gpu_up/reg/va_alloc/map/unmap/submit) for the user client.

